          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"flaubert-madame-bovary-8c91fb38ed76\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":4,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.97,\"analysis\":\"The mother's “Comme je t’aime” strongly avows her loving emotional state while also functioning as an emotionally triggered exclamation. Her rush to embrace the addressee, the exclamatory syntax, and the immediate repetition reinforce E without weakening the clear T force. Nothing indicates a commitment or relational undertaking beyond the expression of affection.\",\"ambiguity\":\"T and E are simultaneously strong: the utterance is both a genuine avowal and an exclamation, rather than clearly reducible to only one mode.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"A mother directly addresses her child in spoken dialogue while rushing to embrace her; the highlighted occurrence is the first of two immediately repeated declarations.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The declaration occurs amid an urgent request to have the child brought to her and a movement to embrace her. “Comme” and the exclamation mark present the love as emotionally overflowing, while “ma pauvre enfant” adds tenderness and concern. The local passage supplies no evidence of deception, irony, or an undertaking with commitment force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Comme je t’aime, ma pauvre enfant!”\",\"supports\":\"The explicit first-person declaration presents maternal love as true (T), while “Comme” and the exclamation mark strongly support exclamatory force (E).\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“dit sa mère se précipitant pour l’embrasser”\",\"supports\":\"The speaker is identified as the addressee's mother, and her rushing to embrace the child supports an emotionally activated, affectionate delivery.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The declaration is immediately repeated: “comme je t’aime!”\",\"supports\":\"The emphatic repetition strengthens the reading of emotionally overflowing avowal and exclamation rather than a distinct undertaking.\",\"confidence\":0.98}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"The combination of strong T and strong E naturally captures the utterance as an exclamatory avowal of maternal love. No important aspect of its core force falls outside T/P/E.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
